{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 373 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "1191e3a9854c9bce121bfbe9fa05a2e3f2ae2452b8edb5a0dc61cbc6df6ca6bf" :edb/db-before-t 372 :edb/db-after-t 373 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533685 50 #inst "2026-10-04T11:28:45.976Z" 13194139533685 true] [17592186175975 1020 #edb/ref 17592186246710 13194139533685 true] [17592186175975 1020 #edb/ref 17592186246717 13194139533685 true] [17592186175975 1020 #edb/ref 17592186246766 13194139533685 true] [17592186175975 1020 #edb/ref 17592186246773 13194139533685 true] [17592186175976 1020 #edb/ref 17592186246724 13194139533685 true] [17592186175976 1020 #edb/ref 17592186246731 13194139533685 true] [17592186175976 1020 #edb/ref 17592186246780 13194139533685 true] [17592186175976 1020 #edb/ref 17592186246787 13194139533685 true] [17592186175976 1020 #edb/ref 17592186246794 13194139533685 true] [17592186175984 1020 #edb/ref 17592186246738 13194139533685 true] [17592186175984 1020 #edb/ref 17592186246745 13194139533685 true] [17592186175984 1020 #edb/ref 17592186246752 13194139533685 true] [17592186175984 1020 #edb/ref 17592186246759 13194139533685 true] [17592186176269 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533685 true] [17592186176269 1145 "First, let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933873/assets/df1aba3f5ff980de82a74dde8170ad708e379caf2188873bcddc83177e87c7a6.png)\n\nOur graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. If we rotate the graph ${180}^{∘}$ around the origin, we get the same picture. This means that $tan⁡x$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡(-x)=-tan⁡x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡(-a) & =-tan⁡a \\\\  & =-(-2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533685 true] [17592186176376 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533685 true] [17592186176376 1145 "Let's plot the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933873/assets/326418398ce1a33f03a21f3bdb58107856f4ccb72241429f1604486281e60822.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function has an asymptote at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and the period is $\\pi .$ Therefore, the asymptotes occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function returns only positive values on the interval $(0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ and the period is $\\pi .$ Therefore, the function is positive on $(n\\pi ,\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi )\\,.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The zeros occur at $x=0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,…,$ which can be written as $x=n\\pi .$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"." 13194139533685 true] [17592186246710 1017 #edb/ref 17592186246711 13194139533685 true] [17592186246710 1089 "q-103289" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246710 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533685 true] [17592186246710 1100 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=tan⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the function is all real numbers except $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi $\n- The function has zeros at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi $ for any integer $n$\n- The range of the function is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{4})$" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246710 1113 #uuid "264dc1d8-6c35-583a-b855-2ee23edf3c8d" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246710 1138 false 13194139533685 true] [17592186246710 1145 "Let's plot the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933873/assets/732955302ca49a41f6c43cf242d7c869e630e88d804c4b56a5beb3b081f2d230.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function is defined everywhere, except where $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is false. The zeros occur at $x=0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,…,$ which can be written as $x=n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function takes values on all the real numbers, hence the range is $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only\"." 13194139533685 true] [17592186246711 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246712 13194139533685 true] [17592186246711 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246713 13194139533685 true] [17592186246711 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246714 13194139533685 true] [17592186246711 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246715 13194139533685 true] [17592186246711 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246716 13194139533685 true] [17592186246711 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533685 true] [17592186246711 1041 "selection" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246711 1104 #edb/ref 17592186246714 13194139533685 true] [17592186246711 1110 #uuid "d3944d1c-16bd-589e-b90e-443fdf8f4cd2" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246712 1034 "II and III only" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246712 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533685 true] [17592186246712 1111 #uuid "44e70e67-040e-58ec-8e2b-2215930016dd" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246713 1034 "I and III only" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246713 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533685 true] [17592186246713 1111 #uuid "c39ea976-b5f9-5004-a552-68c5c025132b" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246714 1034 "I only" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246714 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533685 true] [17592186246714 1111 #uuid "961ce003-6035-5a1f-9aa6-141fd94606dd" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246715 1034 "III only" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246715 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533685 true] [17592186246715 1111 #uuid "749bbc90-2eb3-5bf8-94a4-e98f5302c1c7" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246716 1034 "II only" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246716 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533685 true] [17592186246716 1111 #uuid "b08c447a-cc1d-58c7-87af-7e3ac3d32a74" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246717 1017 #edb/ref 17592186246718 13194139533685 true] [17592186246717 1089 "q-103295" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246717 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533685 true] [17592186246717 1100 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=tan⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ represents any integer.\n\n- The vertical asymptotes of the function are $x=2n\\pi $\n- Its graph passes through the point $(0,0)$\n- $tan⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})=tan⁡(x+\\frac{5\\pi }{6})$" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246717 1113 #uuid "317d2b9c-f42d-5ece-9543-51e9cfb75b9f" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246717 1138 false 13194139533685 true] [17592186246717 1145 "Let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933873/assets/c2d0606829588b01f6cba2fa4785b201c47a6d9ffa325d54e64544c9769d7e4a.png)\n\nLet's examine each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function has an asymptote at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and the period is $\\pi .$ Therefore, the asymptotes occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the graph of the function passes through the point $(0,0).$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function $y=tan⁡x$ has period $\\pi .$ So, $tan⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})=tan⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\pi )=tan⁡(x+\\frac{5\\pi }{6}).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." 13194139533685 true] [17592186246718 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246719 13194139533685 true] [17592186246718 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246720 13194139533685 true] [17592186246718 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246721 13194139533685 true] [17592186246718 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246722 13194139533685 true] [17592186246718 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246723 13194139533685 true] [17592186246718 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533685 true] [17592186246718 1041 "selection" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246718 1104 #edb/ref 17592186246719 13194139533685 true] [17592186246718 1110 #uuid "e8979ad8-23a5-583c-b1b2-f6796537e051" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246719 1034 "II and III only" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246719 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533685 true] [17592186246719 1111 #uuid "e88fdd70-1af2-5d17-af59-4f2afd8ef738" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246720 1034 "I and III only" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246720 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533685 true] [17592186246720 1111 #uuid "22d203ee-ab5a-5dfb-8879-4e89e5cf102d" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246721 1034 "III only" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246721 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533685 true] [17592186246721 1111 #uuid "3ab27600-9377-5b2b-a4b4-dc6697afd59c" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246722 1034 "I and II only" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246722 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533685 true] [17592186246722 1111 #uuid "6adf4eaa-a986-5f83-911e-4759f7bd183f" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246723 1034 "II only" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246723 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533685 true] [17592186246723 1111 #uuid "6e945b93-d364-508a-92fa-2823a1c5dbe4" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246724 1017 #edb/ref 17592186246725 13194139533685 true] [17592186246724 1089 "q-103307" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246724 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533685 true] [17592186246724 1100 "If $tan⁡x=\\frac{1}{3},$ for some value of $x,$ find the value of $12tan⁡(x+5\\pi )-6.$" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246724 1113 #uuid "86a6763e-11cd-57bc-8cd3-73cb100b14e0" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246724 1138 false 13194139533685 true] [17592186246724 1145 "The period of $y=tan⁡x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for any integer $n,$ we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡x=tan⁡(x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=5$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡x=tan⁡(x+5\\cdot \\pi )=tan⁡(x+5\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $tan⁡x=\\frac{1}{3},$ we get that $tan⁡(x+5\\pi )=\\frac{1}{3}.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n12tan⁡(x+5\\pi )-6=12(\\frac{1}{3})-6=4-6=-2.\n$$" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246725 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246726 13194139533685 true] [17592186246725 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246727 13194139533685 true] [17592186246725 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246728 13194139533685 true] [17592186246725 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246729 13194139533685 true] [17592186246725 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246730 13194139533685 true] [17592186246725 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533685 true] [17592186246725 1041 "selection" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246725 1104 #edb/ref 17592186246730 13194139533685 true] [17592186246725 1110 #uuid "e0e1aa4d-b0f0-5fdd-8985-76afd50887a4" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246726 1034 "4\\pi -2" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246726 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533685 true] [17592186246726 1111 #uuid "a8c6e9d2-f837-595b-b2ab-6e30e5afe2e8" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246727 1034 "2" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246727 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533685 true] [17592186246727 1111 #uuid "c474b438-f75e-5326-b86f-ea37380b08b7" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246728 1034 "6" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246728 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533685 true] [17592186246728 1111 #uuid "df77ed1e-085a-511f-b92a-5085944e2627" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246729 1034 "4" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246729 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533685 true] [17592186246729 1111 #uuid "077336e3-2026-52ac-8db5-9ea4440b56ac" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246730 1034 "-2" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246730 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533685 true] [17592186246730 1111 #uuid "e0bb8569-0e94-501e-a382-2594d35f01cf" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246731 1017 #edb/ref 17592186246732 13194139533685 true] [17592186246731 1089 "q-103312" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246731 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533685 true] [17592186246731 1100 "If $tan⁡x=16,$ for some value of $x,$ find the value of $\\frac{3}{4}tan⁡(x-9\\pi ).$" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246731 1113 #uuid "95a5187e-80fa-5229-bf10-a6677dad6740" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246731 1138 false 13194139533685 true] [17592186246731 1145 "The period of $y=tan⁡x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for any integer $n,$ we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡x=tan⁡(x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-9$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡x=tan⁡(x+(-9)\\cdot \\pi )=tan⁡(x-9\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $tan⁡x=16,$ we get that $tan⁡(x-9\\pi )=16.$