46747 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533685 true] [17592186246747 1111 #uuid "6fa05a7d-837f-5014-ab4b-481dce1ee09f" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246748 1034 "3" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246748 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533685 true] [17592186246748 1111 #uuid "2d3ed6f8-2111-582e-a331-1efe7961e0cf" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246749 1034 "-3" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246749 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533685 true] [17592186246749 1111 #uuid "4ad6eab1-520d-5c88-bb91-967a68010b17" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246750 1034 "-\\sqrt{3}" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246750 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533685 true] [17592186246750 1111 #uuid "07ce8ac1-c336-5e8e-be6e-50e7017a127a" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246751 1034 "\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246751 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533685 true] [17592186246751 1111 #uuid "053cecc9-7f20-53ff-9e9a-94dce16ff772" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246752 1017 #edb/ref 17592186246753 13194139533685 true] [17592186246752 1089 "q-158041" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246752 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533685 true] [17592186246752 1100 "If $tan⁡x=-4,$ then $\\frac{1}{2}tan⁡(-x+3\\pi )+3=$" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246752 1113 #uuid "6beda82e-a20a-5d58-a4e3-3ff246d0aab0" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246752 1138 false 13194139533685 true] [17592186246752 1145 "First, let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933873/assets/df1aba3f5ff980de82a74dde8170ad708e379caf2188873bcddc83177e87c7a6.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note the following:\n\n- The period of $tan⁡x$ is $\\pi .$\n\n- Our graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. This means that $tan⁡x$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡(-x)=-tan⁡x.\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate our expression:\n\n- Firstly, using the periodicity of $tan⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡(-x+3\\pi ) & =tan⁡(-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Secondly, using the oddness of $tan⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡(-x) & =-tan⁡x \\\\  & =-(-4) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}tan⁡(-x+3\\pi )+3 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4+3 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2}+3 \\\\  & =2+3 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246753 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246754 13194139533685 true] [17592186246753 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246755 13194139533685 true] [17592186246753 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246756 13194139533685 true] [17592186246753 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246757 13194139533685 true] [17592186246753 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246758 13194139533685 true] [17592186246753 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533685 true] [17592186246753 1041 "selection" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246753 1104 #edb/ref 17592186246758 13194139533685 true] [17592186246753 1110 #uuid "37b92d9e-62b7-5ad8-891c-381fd78cc8b0" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246754 1034 "3" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246754 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533685 true] [17592186246754 1111 #uuid "0091aa30-09bf-5a3f-9b92-18ff012af49d" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246755 1034 "1" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246755 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533685 true] [17592186246755 1111 #uuid "2fe09367-8d58-5cdb-931e-810c1b9b1988" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246756 1034 "0" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246756 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533685 true] [17592186246756 1111 #uuid "6aa2314b-8077-5f5e-aaa8-24f8fe179acb" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246757 1034 "-1" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246757 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533685 true] [17592186246757 1111 #uuid "8a139043-4a92-5b9a-b86c-7c070005be47" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246758 1034 "5" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246758 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533685 true] [17592186246758 1111 #uuid "f9c374c9-b095-5e2c-bc39-0efbed8aa6c0" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246759 1017 #edb/ref 17592186246760 13194139533685 true] [17592186246759 1089 "q-158046" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246759 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533685 true] [17592186246759 1100 "If $tan⁡x=-2,$ then $\\frac{3}{5}tan⁡(-x-7\\pi )+\\frac{4}{5}=$" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246759 1113 #uuid "e8566090-d643-5dbe-8765-e92369416700" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246759 1138 false 13194139533685 true] [17592186246759 1145 "First, let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933873/assets/df1aba3f5ff980de82a74dde8170ad708e379caf2188873bcddc83177e87c7a6.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note the following:\n\n- The period of $tan⁡x$ is $\\pi .$\n\n- Our graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. This means that $tan⁡x$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡(-x)=-tan⁡x.\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate our expression:\n\n- Firstly, using the periodicity of $tan⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡(-x-7\\pi ) & =tan⁡(-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Secondly, using the oddness of $tan⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡(-x) & =-tan⁡x \\\\  & =-(-2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5}tan⁡(-x-7\\pi )+\\frac{4}{5} & =\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot 2+\\frac{4}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{5}+\\frac{4}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{5} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246760 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246761 13194139533685 true] [17592186246760 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246762 13194139533685 true] [17592186246760 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246763 13194139533685 true] [17592186246760 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246764 13194139533685 true] [17592186246760 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246765 13194139533685 true] [17592186246760 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533685 true] [17592186246760 1041 "selection" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246760 1104 #edb/ref 17592186246763 13194139533685 true] [17592186246760 1110 #uuid "5a16fdac-8762-505c-a542-af7c74cd4100" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246761 1034 "-\\frac{2}{5}" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246761 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533685 true] [17592186246761 1111 #uuid "3f4b4477-660e-5714-b505-d0a25a2344b3" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246762 1034 "\\frac{2}{5}" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246762 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533685 true] [17592186246762 1111 #uuid "c1e6cf9f-c1ae-5769-a71d-df1788898d95" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246763 1034 "2" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246763 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533685 true] [17592186246763 1111 #uuid "8dace757-b9ec-56f2-9400-1269df92064b" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246764 1034 "\\pi +\\frac{2}{5}" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246764 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533685 true] [17592186246764 1111 #uuid "9e9d5c41-1c3c-5f72-aed0-00655708ae51" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246765 1034 "-1" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246765 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533685 true] [17592186246765 1111 #uuid "157f0816-893e-5932-b514-0192d3b68646" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246766 1017 #edb/ref 17592186246767 13194139533685 true] [17592186246766 1089 "q-28675" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246766 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533685 true] [17592186246766 1100 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=tan⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ represents any integer.\n\n- $tan⁡(x+\\pi )=tan⁡(x+n\\pi ).$\n- The function has asymptotes at $x=n\\pi $\n- $tan⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=tan⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246766 1113 #uuid "a50a54b2-642a-5810-b035-b477949523f0" 13194139533685 true] [17592186246766 1138 false 13194139533685 true] [17592186246766 1145 "Let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933873/assets/31b430f003171dcc04a8f17402d6035fbbc305c244d3676bbf5da83fa447bd50.png)\n\nLet's examine each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function $y=tan⁡x$ has period $\\pi .$ So, $tan⁡(x+\\pi )=tan⁡(x)=tan⁡(x+n\\pi )$ for any in